From 484a22535b56a13efeebadf51521850b5e28e707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitriy Andreychenko <dmitriy.andreychenko@flant.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:24:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: conntrack import/export HTTP endpoints

GET /conntrack/export streams one IPv4 endpoint's conntrack entries; POST
/conntrack/import ingests them on another node, translating each entry's RevNAT
from the source node's service id to the local one. Carries a VM's established
connections across a live migration.

Ported from daemon/cmd/status.go, which 1.20 removed: the handlers now live in
pkg/maps and are provided by its cell, generated API code comes from
"make generate-api", and the wire format is unchanged so the
Cilium-Conntrack-Export-Version header stays at "1".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
